                <pb facs="0673" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg601"/>

                <head>Grutli Union of Travers</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Travers</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-15">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 15, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Neuenburg, Boudry, Travers,
                    Couvet, Fleurier, and Chaux-de-Fond sections of the Swiss Grutli Union, in their
                    meetings of yesterday, unanimously resolved to approve of the address of
                    sympathy and condolence to the American Union.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, as secretary, has the honor to enclose you the resolution, and
                    subscribe himself your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. STEFFEN, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundesrath</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">in
                            Berne</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
